# Provider binaries and the local backend scratch dir. `.terraform.lock.hcl` IS committed (it pins
# provider versions and their checksums, which is the point); everything else under .terraform/ is a
# ~40MB download that `terraform init` reproduces exactly.
terraform/.terraform/

# `terraform plan -out` artefacts. roles/terraform_apply writes one so that the plan reviewed is
# the plan applied -- it is a binary snapshot of intended changes and has no business in git.
terraform/*.tfplan

# State never lands here at all: the backend is Terraform Cloud (organisation `bitcashier`,
# workspace `kinowo-infra`). These two lines are belt-and-braces against a stray
# `terraform init -migrate-state` or a local-backend experiment, because a committed state file
# leaks every attribute the providers read back -- and on this fleet that includes secrets.
terraform/terraform.tfstate
terraform/terraform.tfstate.backup
